ERROR	effect.format-suspends	compiler/tests/typecheck/golden/format_suspends.saw:21:10	`Printable.format` must not suspend, and `format_suspends.Meter`'s does: `Meter.format` → `settle` → `yield_now` (parks the task). A render (an interpolation, a `{}` argument of `print`, `panic` or `assert`, `print(x)`, `try!`'s message and `to_string()`) calls `format` synchronously into stack scratch, where nothing may suspend and a `blocking` extern cannot be offloaded, so `format` is `sync`. Do the suspending work first, in a method of its own, and render what it returns
